      ],
      "message": "test: AutoFile/BufferedFile I/O failures discard the OS error\n\nAutoFile::write(), write_buffer(), read() (via detail_fread), ignore(),\nand BufferedFile::Fill() throw a fixed, generic message on a genuine\nfread()/fwrite() failure (as opposed to reaching end-of-file),\ndiscarding the errno that explains why the call actually failed.\n\nForce such a failure by opening a file in the wrong direction (write\nto a read-only stream, read from a write-only one) and confirm the\nresulting exception's message does not carry the OS error.\n\nTODO: flip check_io_failure() to assert the OS error IS present once\nAutoFile/BufferedFile are fixed to include it.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "pablomartin4btc",
        "email": "pablomartin4btc@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-09T19:31:27Z"
